===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# The [[measurement]] of [[time]], or [[determining]] what the [[local]] time is.
# The quality of being punctual, keeping to a set time.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=May|author=R. K. Kirkland|title=The Cavan & Leitrim Railway|journal=Railway Magazine|page=343|text='''Timekeeping''' is better than on many Irish main lines; indeed, such delays as do occur are often attributable to late running of the Dublin-Sligo trains.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1959|month=March|author=D. Bertram|title=An old friend - the 9.7|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=141|text=As already indicated, '''timekeeping''' is very poor. Point-to-point times are not kept, even with a clear road, and whilst fast running has never been a feature of the route because of the large number of junctions and speed restrictions, this Sunday night lethargy is hard to explain.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1961|month=October|title=Motive Power Miscellany: Scottish Region|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=638|text=Our correspondent found that '''timekeeping''' had suffered following the substitution of Class 5 [[4-6-0]]s on these workings.}}

